# 2026-03-06 01:18:48.557117
+Read PROJECT_CONTEXT.md first.
+
+Then analyze the entire repository.
+
+Project rules:
+- Never break the /home page.
+- Never remove Moonraker communication.
+- Never delete working functionality unless absolutely necessary.
+- Work in very small safe steps.
+- Always explain the plan before editing files.
+- After each step create a git commit with a clear message.
+- Never refactor large parts of the project in one step.
+
+Technical context:
+This project is a touchscreen UI for a Klipper/Moonraker controlled cutting machine.
+
+The UI is written in:
+- SvelteKit
+- Vite
+- TypeScript
+
+Moonraker communication happens through the existing /moonraker proxy.
+
+Machine constraints:
+- X travel: 100 mm
+- Y travel: 100 mm
+- Z handled separately
+- Only X and Y are used for shape cutting.
+
+Current UI pages:
+- /home → machine status + macros
+- /manual → manual jogging
+- /shape → parametric shape cutting
+- /dxf → DXF cutting (later)
+- /settings → machine settings
+
+Current goal:
+Implement the complete shape cutting pipeline.
+
+Steps you should implement:
+
+1. Inspect src/routes/shape/+page.svelte
+2. Implement a G-code generator for:
+   - circle
+   - rectangle
+   - hexagon
+   - slot
+
+3. The generator must:
+   - respect the 100mm XY limits
+   - produce safe incremental moves
+   - generate valid Klipper G-code
+
+4. When the user presses "Vorm snijden":
+   - generate the G-code
+   - send it to Moonraker using the existing API structure
+
+5. The system must:
+   - show machine status from Moonraker
+   - show real error messages
+   - show "Ready to cut"
+   - later wait for a physical start button (prepare placeholder)
+
+Workflow:
+Before editing anything:
+- list which files you will modify
+- explain the plan
+
+Then implement step by step.
+
+Do NOT start coding yet.
+First analyze the repository and describe the next safe development step.

