# 2026-03-06 16:39:35.826003
+Fix the on-screen numeric keypad behavior in the shape page.
+
+Required behavior:
+- When the keypad opens, the top display field must always start empty.
+- The keypad input must behave like a text input for decimal numbers.
+- Clear must fully empty the keypad display.
+- Backspace must remove the last typed character.
+- Only one decimal separator is allowed.
+- Maximum 2 digits after the decimal point.
+- Typing "." as the first character should result in "0.".
+- Pressing Enter must parse the typed value and write it into the selected target field.
+- If the entered value is below the allowed minimum, clamp it to the minimum.
+- If the entered value is above the allowed maximum, clamp it to the maximum.
+- If Enter is pressed while the keypad display is empty, do not change the original field value.
+- The original field value must not change while typing; only update it on Enter.
+- The keypad display must show only the currently typed string, not the existing field value.
+
+Implementation notes:
+- Separate the temporary keypad input string from the actual numeric field value.
+- Use a string state like keypadInput for typing.
+- Use a target object containing field name, min, max and decimals.
+- Validate input so that only digits and one decimal point are allowed, with max 2 decimals.
+- On Enter, convert keypadInput to number, clamp, round to max 2 decimals, then assign to the target field.

